<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Altmühl</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Altmühl is a river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, a left tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> about 220 kilometres long. It flows through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a> past Treuchtlingen, Pappenheim and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eichstatt">Eichstätt</a> in a winding limestone valley, now the Altmühl Valley Nature Park, and joins the Danube at Kelheim. Its lower course forms part of the Main–Danube Canal.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/altmuhl.jpg" alt="Altmühl" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jacquesverlaeken · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Essing_Altm%C3%BChl2009_P1020203.jpeg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
